      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ending a narrative with a character succumbing to despair forces the reader to confront the gravity of that experience, which can be profoundly truthful. Whether it's a \"cop out\" depends entirely on the tone you wish to set for your story. If your theme is the weariness of existence, a bleak conclusion offers a stark, uncompromising honesty. Conversely, if your goal is to explore the endurance of the human spirit, a different resolution might serve the story's core argument better.",
